## Why This Is Asked
Tests DP with a spacing constraint and path reconstruction, a common interview variation.

## Key Concepts
- DP over prefix with constrained subsequences
- 2D state and reconstruction pointers
- Handling infeasible states and space-time trade-offs

## Code Example
```javascript
// state definitions: dp[i][t], par[i][t]
function solve(A, n, k, d) {
  const NEG = -1e15;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  const par = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  for (let i=1; i<=n; i++) dp[i][1] = A[i-1];
  for (let t=2; t<=k; t++) {
    for (let i=1; i<=n; i++) {
      // skip i
      if (dp[i-1][t] > dp[i][t]) { dp[i][t] = dp[i-1][t]; par[i][t] = -1; }
      // take i
      if (i - d >= 1 && dp[i-d][t-1] !== NEG) {
        const val = dp[i-d][t-1] + A[i-1];
        if (val > dp[i][t]) { dp[i][t] = val; par[i][t] = i-d; }
      }
    }
  }
  return {dp, par};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you reconstruct the indices from par to return the actual solution?
- How can you optimize space without changing asymptotic time?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to model partitioning with a simple per-block objective and reconstruct optimal cuts. It reveals DP formulation, range queries, and backtracking.

## Key Concepts
- Partition DP across two dimensions (prefix and blocks)
- Range maximum precomputation or on-the-fly tracking
- Backpointers for path reconstruction
- Time/space trade-offs and potential optimizations

## Code Example
```javascript
function minPartitionCostMax(A, m){
  const n = A.length;
  // precompute max for all ranges
  const rangeMax = Array.from({length: n}, () => Array(n).fill(0));
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++){
    let cur = 0;
    for(let j=i;j<n;j++){
      cur = Math.max(cur, A[j]);
      rangeMax[i][j] = cur;
    }
  }
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(m+1).fill(Infinity));
  const par = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(m+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    for(let j=1;j<=Math.min(i,m);j++){
      for(let t=j-1; t<=i-1; t++){
        const val = dp[t][j-1] + rangeMax[t][i-1];
        if(val < dp[i][j]){
          dp[i][j] = val;
          par[i][j] = t;
        }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruct
  const cuts = [];
  let i = n, j = m;
  while(j>0){
    const t = par[i][j];
    cuts.push(i);
    i = t;
    j--;
  }
  cuts.reverse();
  return {cost: dp[n][m], partitions: cuts};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you optimize to O(n m) time using monotonic queues?  
- How would you adapt if each chapter cost were max(A[t..i-1]) + c*(i-t)?

## Why This Is Asked
New DP angle focusing on subarray range gain with exact k partitions.

## Key Concepts
- DP partitioning
- Precomputing range max/min
- Reconstruction through pointers
- Time: O(n^2 k); Space: O(nk)

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxGainKSubarrays(A, k){
  const n = A.length;
  const gain = Array.from({length:n}, ()=>Array(n).fill(0));
  for(let l=0;l<n;l++){
    let mn = A[l], mx = A[l];
    for(let r=l;r<n;r++){
      mn = Math.min(mn, A[r]);
      mx = Math.max(mx, A[r]);
      gain[l][r] = mx - mn;
    }
  }
  const dp = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const take = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=>Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    for(let t=0;t<=Math.min(i,k);t++){
      dp[i][t] = dp[i-1][t];
      take[i][t] = take[i-1][t];
      if(t>0){
        for(let l=1;l<=i;l++){
          const val = dp[l-1][t-1] + gain[l-1][i-1];
          if(val>dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t] = val; take[i][t] = l-1; }
        }
      }
    }
  }
  const res = [];
  let i=n, t=k;
  while(t>0){
    const lminus1 = take[i][t];
    const l = lminus1 + 1;
    res.unshift([l, i]);
    i = lminus1; t--;
  }
  return {score: dp[n][k], blocks: res};
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you optimize memory to O(nk) and still reconstruct blocks?
- How would the solution change if subarrays must have at least a fixed length L?

